        <div class="jcBand">
            <div id="pnlJobDescription">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p>Secure California&#39;s Future,&nbsp;Join the Homeland Security Policy Team: Become a Homeland Security Policy Coordinator&nbsp;at the California Governor&#39;s Office of Emergency Services (Cal OES).</p><p>From raging wildfires to the unprecedented COVID-19 pandemic, California has faced numerous emergencies that have impacted millions of lives. We are seeking driven individuals to join our team and help shape policies that safeguard the state&#39;s critical infrastructure and enhance emergency preparedness.</p><p>Join our dynamic team as a Staff Services Manager I (Specialist) supporting statewide engagement in critical homeland security programs. The Office of Homeland Security Policy plays an important role in strengthening California’s homeland security enterprise through strategic policy development, stakeholder coordination, and data-driven decision making. This role involves providing guidance to various stakeholders on HSD initiatives and offering executive-level support to develop and recommend strategies and policies aligned with division-wide goals. Please review the duty statement for more information. Key responsibilities of this positions include, but are not limited to:</p><ul>
			<li>Independently manages and oversees the implementation of Homeland Security Division programs and initiatives, including the development and continuous evaluation of the State Homeland Security Strategy.</li><li>Conducts complex policy analysis to identify emerging trends, potential threats, and innovative solutions to enhance homeland security effectiveness.</li><li>Evaluates program needs, recommend and implement necessary changes to ensure program effectiveness and compliance with applicable laws, regulations, and best practices.</li><li>Serves as the primary point of contact for critical homeland security programs, providing expert guidance to stakeholders and facilitating effective communication across all levels of government.</li><li>Conducts complex research and analysis on homeland security issues, preparing comprehensive reports, policy briefs, and analytical documents for agency leadership and stakeholders.</li><li>Conducts briefings for executives and homeland security partners on programmatic updates and emerging issues and provide logistical support for meetings and events.</li></ul>
		<p>If you’re ready to contribute to California’s homeland security through policy initiatives and strategic collaborations, we want to hear from you!</p><p>This position is located at our Mather Campus and is eligible for a hybrid work schedule which may include up to one day of remote work per week. Additional in-office days may be required based on business needs.</p><p>The position is a 12-month limited term (LT) and may be extended up to 24 months or become permanent. </p><p>This is a readvertisement. If you have previously applied, your application is still under consideration, and there is no need to reapply.</p><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=26506953&name=163-400-4800-904Proposed.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
</div>

            <div id="pnlWorkingConditions">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Working Conditions</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p><strong>DMV Pull Program</strong><br />Participation in the DMV Pull Program is required. The position(s) require(s) a valid Driver’s License (DL). You must answer the questions addressing your DL on your application. Ensure you provide your DL number, class, expiration date, and any endorsements and/or restrictions.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Conflict of Interest</strong><br />This position is designated under the Conflict-of-Interest Code and is required to complete Form 700 within 30 days of appointment. Failure to comply with the Conflict-of-Interest Code requirements may void the appointment. </p><p>See duty statement for more information.</p>
                </p>
            
</div>
